{
  "_comment": [
    "Semantic classes for CitySample, and the rules that assign them. Edit freely: ids must be unique,",
    "1-253 (0 is 'unlabeled', and is everything no rule matches). Colors are for the viewer only.",
    "",
    "Three kinds of rule, most specific first (Tempo's labeler resolves a component before its actor):",
    "  static_mesh_patterns / skeletal_mesh_patterns: Python regexes over a mesh's full asset path.",
    "    Applied at runtime to the meshes that are actually loaded, as World Partition streams them in,",
    "    so a rule can be broad without loading anything. A component whose mesh matches is labeled on",
    "    its own, whatever its actor's class. Classes are tried in file order; the first match wins.",
    "  component_tags: a component carrying the tag; beats every mesh rule. The client tags each of the",
    "    ego vehicle's components 'TempoEgo' at runtime, so its body isn't labeled by its van/car mesh.",
    "  actor_tags: an actor carrying the tag. The client tags the ego vehicle itself 'TempoEgo' too.",
    "  actor_classes: an actor of the class or a subclass (the most-derived match wins). Paths the",
    "    packaged build doesn't have are dropped with a warning, rather than failing the whole table.",
    "",
    "Run the client with --coverage to list the loaded meshes no rule matched."
  ],
  "classes": [
